bn al-Muthannā) and one «وحدثنيه» route (Fadl b. Sahl) carry the same saying; written out in full because the Fadl route repeats Nafi' and Ibn Umar with its own names, so one shared tail cannot cover both","«كل هؤلاء عن نافع، عن ابن عمر» is read as the common end of the six branches; it is written into each of them","«بمثل حديث مالك وابن جريج» and «إلا ابن جريج وحده» name other transmitters for the same saying: a variant group, never a route","«وقد تابع ابن جريج على ذلك ابن إسحاق» names Ibn Ishaq as following Ibn Jurayj in wording: a variant group","«- يعني ابن حازم -», «- رضى الله عنهما -» are glosses, left out; «ولم يقل أحد منهم ... سمعت» is wording only; «فذكر بمثله» refers back to the saying"],"fixes":[]}
